   "k": "final claims text",
   "v": "BRCA1 is associated with familial cancer of breast, familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1, pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4, and Fanconi anemia complementation group S.⁠1–4 Found 4 disease records for BRCA1: Familial cancer of breast, Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1, Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 and Fanconi anemia complementation group S.⁠1–4\n\nDISEASE ASSOCIATIONS AND INHERITED RISK\n\nBRCA1 mutations are responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers.⁠23 The gene encodes a 190 kD nuclear phosphoprotein that functions as a tumor suppressor and maintains genomic stability through the BRCA1-associated genome surveillance complex.⁠23\n\nDISEASE RECORDS FOUND\nDISEASE\tIDENTIFIER\t\nFamilial cancer of breast\tMedGen:C0346153\t⁠1\nFamilial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1\tMedGen:C2676676\t⁠2\nPancreatic cancer susceptibility 4\tMedGen:C3280442\t⁠3\nFanconi anemia complementation group S\tMedGen:C4554406\t⁠4\nGENE RECORDS FOUND\nGENE\tIDENTIFIER\t\nBRCA1\tNCBIGene:672\t⁠5, 9\nPUBMED RECORDS FOUND\nPAPER\tIDENTIFIER\t\nBRCA1: An Endocrine and Metabolic Regulator.\tPMID:35432218\t⁠6\nPreneoplastic stromal cells promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis.\tPMID:36914836\t⁠11\nBRCA1 safeguards genome integrity by activating chromosome asynapsis checkpoint to eliminate recombination-defective oocytes.\tPMID:38696471\t⁠14\nMechanism of BRCA1-BARD1 function in DNA end resection and DNA protection.\tPMID:39261728\t⁠17\nTargeting GPX4-mediated ferroptosis protection sensitizes BRCA1-deficient cancer cells to PARP inhibitors.\tPMID:39265497\t⁠20\nCLINVAR RECORDS FOUND\nVARIANT\tIDENTIFIER\t\nNM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5243_5277+2788del\tVCV000267740\t⁠7\nNM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5277+2916_5277+2946delinsGG\tVCV000267741\t⁠12\nNG_005905.2:g.(147057_150288)_(160933_166866)del\tVCV000373892\t⁠15\nGRCh37/hg19 17q21.31(chr17:41267743-41267796)x3\tVCV004823850\t⁠18\nNM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.2145C>G (p.Thr715=)\tVCV004848411\t⁠21\nOMIM RECORDS FOUND\nRECORD\tIDENTIFIER\t\nBRCA1 DNA REPAIR-ASSOCIATED PROTEIN; BRCA1\tomim 113705\t⁠8\nCLINICAL TRIAL RECORDS FOUND\nTRIAL\tIDENTIFIER\tSTATUS\t\nGermline BRCA1 and BRCA2 Mutations in Jewish Women Affected by Breast Cancer\tNCT00590109\tCOMPLETED\t⁠10\nBRCA1 Haploinsufficiency and Gene Expression\tNCT00597987\tCOMPLETED\t⁠13\nStudy to Evaluate Treatment Customized According to RAP80 and BRCA1 in Patients With Advanced Lung Carcinoma\tNCT00617656\tTERMINATED\t⁠16\nLetrozole in Preventing Breast Cancer in Postmenopausal Women With a BRCA1 or BRCA2 Mutation\tNCT00673335\tCOMPLETED\t⁠19\nRecombinant Human Chorionic Gonadotropin in Preventing Breast Cancer in Premenopausal Women With BRCA1 Mutations\tNCT00700778\tTERMINATED\t⁠22"
  },
